'' RUN: array slices, P1 (docs/tiko-slices RFC-0003) -- 'a(lo to hi)' over a fixed array, a
'' dynamic array and an 'a()' parameter; 'a(i to i)(0)' is 'a(i)' for every i; empty; re-slice;
'' len, lbound, ubound (dimensions 0 and 2 as fbc gives a one-dimensional array); a write
'' through to the source; passed and returned by value; an unallocated array; string and UDT
'' elements; a const span over a const array. A span is three words.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -w all tests/codegen/src/array-slices.tiko -o tests/codegen/arrayslices.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: warning
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/arrayslices.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/arrayslices.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: fixed 3: 20 30 40
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bounds 0 2 1 1 0-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: write 99
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: singletrue
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: empty 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: reslice 2: 99 40
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dynamic 4: 1 4 9 16
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: param 4: 1 4 9 16
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: returned 3: 1 4 9
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: unallocated 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: strings bob! cy bob!
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: udt 7 24
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: const 2
